{"v":1,"ts":"2026-09-17T06:33:24Z","run":"implementation-routing-analysis-model-20260917-557ea5","activity":"implementation","event":"contradicted","src":"REF-troubleshooting#check-order","note":"check-order 5 reads: 'py -m unittest discover -s tests -v로 회귀 테스트를 실행한다.' That command resolves adaptive_model_router through sys.path, so an installed copy answers the import and the suite verifies a build that is not the working tree. Observed today: 45 of 47 passed against a stale site-packages copy while the two new Claude-provider tests errored with 'module does not have the attribute load_current_claude_config' and 'evaluate_hook() got an unexpected keyword argument provider'; the identical command with src/ prepended gave 47/47 with no file edited. The step therefore certifies the installed build, and its failure mode reads as broken new tests. Replaced in README and CI with py run_tests.py, plus tests/test_environment.py as a loader guard."}
